---
title: App Withdrawal State Machine
---

stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> REQUESTED: actor opens withdrawal flow

  REQUESTED --> DEACTIVATION_PENDING: actor confirms withdrawal intent
  REQUESTED --> CANCELLED: actor abandons before deactivation
  REQUESTED --> FAILED: request failed

  DEACTIVATION_PENDING --> DISCARDED: logical deletion active and purge scheduled
  DEACTIVATION_PENDING --> FAILED: scheduling failed

  DISCARDED --> RECOVERED: actor recovers inside recovery window
  DISCARDED --> TERMINATED: purge job anonymizes after retention
  DISCARDED --> FAILED: recovery or purge failed

  note right of DEACTIVATION_PENDING
    This is the processing state after explicit
    confirmation and before logical deletion becomes
    active. It replaces the ambiguous CLOSING name.
  end note

  note right of DISCARDED
    Retention-window expiry is not EXPIRED here.
    It resolves through purge/anonymization into
    TERMINATED.
  end note

  RECOVERED --> [*]
  TERMINATED --> [*]
  CANCELLED --> [*]
  FAILED --> [*]
